# Permission Matrix & Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) Plan

## Overview
As BrickSetu expands from single-admin usage to multi-user brick kiln management, operational responsibilities are distributed across key staff roles (e.g., Owner, Munshi/Manager, Accountant, Dispatch Clerk, Field Supervisor). 

This plan outlines a **centralized, granular Permission Matrix Architecture**. It defines exact functional access per role across all system modules and details how permissions will be enforced cleanly across the database, server API layer, and frontend UI.

---

## 1. Brick Kiln Operational Roles

| Role Key | Role Name (Local Label) | Description & Key Responsibilities |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `SUPER_ADMIN` | **मालिक (Owner / Super Admin)** | Unrestricted control over all financial, operational, rate, and user settings. |
| `MANAGER` | **मुंशी (Manager / Head Munshi)** | Manages daily labor, moulding counts, daily work logs, and routine operational entries. |
| `ACCOUNTANT` | **कॅशियर (Accountant / Cashier)** | Manages cash/bank advances, party payments, settlements, and expense tracking. |
| `DISPATCH_CLERK` | **गेटकीपर (Dispatch / Sales Clerk)** | Handles customer sales, truck loading dispatches, and gate pass generation. |
| `FIELD_SUPERVISOR` | **पाथरोड सुपरवायजर (Field Supervisor)** | Mobile-optimized logging of daily counts for assigned categories (Kacha/Pakka Maal, Jalai). |

